  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Scattered showers tonight with a chance of\nthunderstorms over the Piedmont. \n\nSurface cold front along the western slopes of the Appalachians\nwill slowly move east tonight. A wave of low pressure is\nforecast to develop along the front late tonight and move up \nthrough the Piedmont and Tidewater areas Friday before clearing\nthe coast Friday night. \n \nRainfall amounts tonight and Friday are expected to range from \n0.2 to 0.5 along and east of Highway 29 with little or no \nmeasurable rain west of the Blue Ridge.  \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Clearing for the weekend; turning breezy and\ncooler. \n\nLingering upper level trough may produce cloudiness over WV and\nthe VA Highlands into the weekend with some sprinkles or \nflurries, but for the most part expecting a drying trend over \nthe weekend and into next week. Winds will also increase as \ncooler air advects into the region Friday night. \n\nIn general expecting near normal temperatures this weekend then\nmoderating early next week.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3: Mainly dry next week with moderating\ntemperatures before late week tumble.\n\nModel ensembles are in general agreement for dry conditions next\nweek and moderating temperatures. There are some differences \nwith respect to a southern stream feature that may pass well \nsouth of the area but it looks as though it will remain \nsuppressed to along the Gulf coast with cloud/rain impacts to \nSouth Texas and across the Gulf towards Florida. Late in the \nweek a northern stream trough is progged to drop south from\nCanada, passing over the Great Lakes. Track of this feature may\nbring a shot of cold air to our region by the following \nweekend...but no significant QPF is advertised attm.",
